# Third-party CAD, kept as it was downloaded.
#
# `tools/gpu sync` runs `git diff --cached --check` before it commits, which
# is worth having over source: it catches trailing whitespace and conflict
# markers before they travel. These files are neither. They are STEP, STL and
# DXF exports from somebody else's tool, thousands of lines of trailing
# spaces by format, and the check on them blocked three commits in a row —
# quietly, because the output was long enough that the reason scrolled past
# and the failure was swallowed by a pipe.
#
# Marked binary: git stops diffing them, stops checking their whitespace, and
# stops pretending a STEP file has lines somebody wrote.
hardware/reference/** -text -diff
*.DXF -text -diff
*.STL -text -diff
*.x_t -text -diff
